### Response Parameters

{% include '_generic_v4_response.md.j2' %}

#### data

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| approval_task_id | string | Approval task ID |
| title | string | Ticket title, such as "Fast execute script - BlueKing - 37 execute objects" |
| risk_level | string | Risk level derived from dangerous-rule matches and target scale. It is **only a hint for the approver and does not take part in the release checks**. Options: `HIGH` (a dangerous script rule was matched, or a high-risk account such as root is used), `MEDIUM` (large target scale, or the target contains dynamic groups or topology nodes), `LOW` (low) |
| operation_type | string | Operation type. Options: `FAST_EXECUTE_SCRIPT` (fast execute script), `FAST_TRANSFER_FILE` (fast transfer file), `EXECUTE_JOB_PLAN` (launch a job plan), `CREATE_JOB_PLAN` (create a job plan), `SAVE_CRON` (save a cron job), `UPDATE_CRON_STATUS` (enable or disable a cron job) |
| bk_scope_type | string | Resource scope type. Options: `biz` (business), `biz_set` (business set) |
| bk_scope_id | string | Resource scope ID, corresponding to `bk_scope_type`, that is the business ID or the business set ID |
| creator | string | Creator of the approval task. The approver must be the creator, and the channel must verify this |
| expire_at | long | Expiry moment of the approval task, Unix timestamp in milliseconds. After expiry the task can no longer be released |
| sections | array | Sections of the ticket content, containing at least the summary section and the raw parameters section |

##### sections[] element

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| key | string | Section key. Options: `summary` (summary section, listing the resolved actual impact), `raw_params` (raw parameters section, the full request parameters) |
| title | string | Section title |
| collapsed | boolean | Rendering hint. Options: `true` (collapse by default is suggested), `false` (expand by default is suggested). Expanding everything does not affect correctness when the channel does not support collapsing |
| fields | array | Fields inside the section |

##### sections[].fields[] element

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| label | string | Display name of the field |
| value | string | Field value. It is only a placeholder and carries no real value when `sensitive` is `true` |
| sensitive | boolean | Whether the field is sensitive. Options: `true` (the server has replaced it with a placeholder), `false` (the real value) |
| highlight | boolean | Whether the field is a high-risk item that must be highlighted, such as a root account, a matched dangerous script rule or a dynamic group target. Options: `true` (highlight it), `false` (ordinary field) |
